      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we first need to determine the total distance covered. We know that the odometer reading on Ryosuke's car was 74,568 miles when he picked his friend up, and it was 74,592 miles when he dropped his friend off. Therefore, the distance covered, denoted as $D$, is $D = 74,592-74,568 = 24$ miles. \n\nNext, we need to calculate the amount of gas used. We know that Ryosuke's car gets 28 miles per gallon, so the amount of gas used, denoted as $G$, is $G = \\dfrac{D}{28} = \\dfrac{24}{28} = \\dfrac{6}{7}$ gallons.\n\nFinally, we need to calculate the cost of the gas used. We know that the price of one gallon of gas is $\\$4.05$, so the cost of the gas used, denoted as $C$, is $C = G \\times \\$4.05 = \\dfrac{6}{7} \\times \\$4.05 = \\dfrac{6 \\times 4.05}{7} = \\dfrac{24.3}{7} \\approx 3.47$.\n\nTherefore, the cost of the gas used for Ryosuke to drive his friend back home from work is $\\boxed{\\$3.47}$.",
